You're on the main square of Mech-City. People bustle about like ants, going about their errands. You can visit many interesting places, but the most important thing is not to miss the approaching time.

On the western edge of the square, you can see the house of the famous Mech-City huntsman Beobras Beowulf, the father of your friend Conan. You can drop in to see him if you like; Conan will certainly want to join you. 

There is a library in the northwest where you can look for something interesting, something that may prove useful. 

In the northeast, there is the house of the inventor Nikolas Swift, the father of your friend Doyle. Doyle is probably at home because he likes to spend his free time in his father's workshop. They say knowledge is power; maybe it's wise to invite him to go with you. 

The house of traveler Cyrus Paganel is on the eastern edge of the square. It is he who was on Wild Island, and he can tell you something that is not written even in Doyle's books. 

You can also return home and stay there for a while, or go to the place where Wild Island is expected to float and just wait for its approach. It's up to you to decide.